<% content_for(:title) { "Deleting your account - Conduit" } %>

<div class="prose max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <h1>Deleting your Conduit account</h1>

  <p>You can delete your account yourself, at any time, from the app or the website.</p>

  <h2>In the app or on the website</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in to your community on Conduit.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>Account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Delete account</strong>, type your email address to confirm, and delete it.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>If you can't sign in</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:ian@colecoding.com">ian@colecoding.com</a> from the address on your account, naming your community, and we'll delete it within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>What's deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account: your name, email address, password and sign-in links, and the phones registered for notifications.</li>
    <li>What's yours alone: your comments, likes, meal RSVPs and sign-ups, the tasks you made, and your notifications.</li>
    <li>Your chat account is deactivated, so you can no longer be reached or signed in to chat.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What stays with your community</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Shared things you added, like documents, decisions and meals, stay for the rest of your community, no longer linked to you.</li>
    <li>Messages you sent in community chat stay in the conversation.</li>
    <li>Encrypted backups keep a copy for up to 30 days, then it's gone.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>See the <%= link_to "privacy policy", privacy_path %> for more on how Conduit handles your information.</p>
</div>
